..Body
Whereas, The South Barton Bridge serves as a key connection along the Border to Border Trail and is located near the recently completed Barton–Bandemer Pedestrian Tunnel;

Whereas, The bridge has experienced deterioration of its steel support structure and has reached the end of its useful life;

Whereas, The condition of the bridge requires replacement of the structure, providing an opportunity to bring the bridge up to current shared-use path design standards and improve the overall trail and park user experience;

Whereas, Parks staff solicited proposals through Request for Proposals #26-37 through the City’s Procurement Unit;

Whereas, Following review of the five proposals and interviews with three firms, staff selected OHM Advisors, Inc. based on its qualifications, relevant experience, proposed work plan, and fee;

Whereas, OHM Advisors, Inc. will subcontract Materials Testing Consultants for geotechnical services;

Whereas, The proposed engineering services will be performed on an hourly, not-to-exceed basis;

Whereas, The total not-to-exceed fee for engineering services is $370,749.00;

Whereas, OHM Advisors, Inc. can meet the project requirements, has submitted all required Non-Discrimination, Living Wage, and Conflict of Interest Disclosure forms, and complies with the requirements of the City’s Non-Discrimination and Living Wage ordinances;

Whereas, Funding is available from the Park Maintenance and Capital Improvement Millage Fund;

Whereas, The City will be awarded a $500,000.00 grant from the Ralph C. Wilson, Jr. Trails Maintenance Fund at the Community Foundation for Southeast Michigan that may be applied to the project; and

Whereas, The Park Advisory Commission recommended approval of the Professional Services Agreement at its September 15, 2026 meeting;

RESOLVED, That City Council approves entering a Professional Services Agreement with OHM Advisors, Inc. in the amount of $370,749.00 for engineering services for the South Barton Bridge Project (RFP #26-37); 

RESOLVED, That a 10% contingency amount of $37,075.00 is established within the project budget to cover potential additional services for the life of the project and that the City Administrator is authorized to approve amendments to the Professional Services Agreement with OHM Advisors, Inc., not to exceed the contingency amount, in order to satisfactorily complete the project; 

RESOLVED, That all amounts herein are without regard to fiscal year; 

RESOLVED, That the Mayor and City Clerk are authorized and directed to execute the agreement after approval by the City Administrator and City Attorney; and

RESOLVED, That the City Administrator is authorized to take all appropriate actions to implement this resolution and the agreement, including execution of subagreements, change orders, or related documents, and to make all determinations and exercise all authority delegated to the City under the agreement.
